    <!--
        ACCEPTED RISK — io.grpc 1.57.2 — CVE-2023-44487 (HTTP/2 Rapid Reset Attack):
        gRPC 1.57.2 is a transitive dependency of ML Kit barcode scanning SDK.
        This app uses gRPC exclusively as a CLIENT (no gRPC server is hosted).
        CVE-2023-44487 is a server-side DoS attack that requires an attacker to flood
        a gRPC server with HTTP/2 RESET frames. A client-only Android app cannot be
        attacked via this vector. No gRPC server is exposed.
        The newer grpc 1.69.1 is also present but Google's ML Kit still pulls 1.57.2.
        Monitor: https://github.com/grpc/grpc-java/security/advisories
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            Accepted risk: CVE-2023-44487 (HTTP/2 Rapid Reset) on io.grpc 1.57.2.
            This app uses gRPC as a CLIENT only (via ML Kit barcode scanning).
            No gRPC server is instantiated — server-side DoS attack not applicable.
            gRPC 1.57.2 is a transitive dep of ML Kit SDK (no direct control).
            Monitor for updated ML Kit SDK that bundles patched gRPC.
            Reviewed: 07-Jun-2026
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/io\.grpc/grpc.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2023-44487</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        ACCEPTED RISK — kotlin-parcelize-runtime — CVE-2025-29903:
        The Parcelize runtime is used for Android IPC serialization (Intent/Bundle data).
        CVE-2025-29903 describes a deserialization vulnerability in Kotlin's parcelize
        runtime that could be exploited if a malicious Parcel is crafted and delivered
        to the app. However:
        1. Lumina does not accept arbitrary Parcel data from external/untrusted sources.
        2. Android's IPC mechanism delivers Parcels only from trusted system processes
           and the app's own components (same UID boundary).
        3. The kotlin version in use is 2.3.10; the flagged 2.2.21 jar is a transitive
           dependency from a third-party SDK — no direct control.
        Monitor: https://youtrack.jetbrains.com/issue/KT- for Kotlin security advisories.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            Accepted risk: CVE-2025-29903 on kotlin-parcelize-runtime.
            Lumina does not receive Parcel data from untrusted external sources.
            Android IPC delivers Parcels only from trusted system processes (same UID boundary).
            The 2.2.21 jar is a transitive dep from a third-party SDK (no direct control).
            Monitor JetBrains security advisories for Kotlin runtime patches.
            Reviewed: 07-Jun-2026
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.jetbrains\.kotlin/kotlin-parcelize-runtime@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2025-29903</cve>
    </suppress>

